  "english": "6. Sunday. Tone 3 [GDz]. Third [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 2 [B]: \"Who art the King\" (Որ թագաւորդ ես). Lord I Have Cried Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [GDz]: \"Glorified\" (Փառաւորեալ). Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of Saint James.\n\n9. Wednesday. Tone 8 [DK]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n\n13. Sunday. Tone 4 [BK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 4 [BK]: \"Who [humbled Himself] to the form of a servant\" (Որ զծառայի). Lord I Have Cried Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [BK]: \"They anticipated\" (Կանխեցին).\n\n20. Sunday. Tone 3 [BDz]. Fifth [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 5 [GDz]: \"Glorified Son\" (Փառաւորեալ որդի). Lord I Have Cried Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [B]: \"Upon the tomb\" (Ի գերեզման), to the end.\n\n21. Monday. Tone 4 [BK]. Saints Abraham and Khoren, and Saints Cosmas and Damian. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 8 [OK]: \"Holy God\" (Սուրբ աստուած).\n\n22. Tuesday. Tone 5 [GDz]. Saint Adeodatus [Asduadzadur] the Martyr. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 2 [AK]: \"Who art exalted\" (Որ բարձրեալդ ես).\n\n24. Thursday. Tone 7 [DDz]. David the Prophet, and James the Apostle.\n\n27. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Sixth [Sunday]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Before all eternity\" (Նախայաւիտեան). Lord I Have Cried Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [AK]: \"Wondrous Resurrection\" (Հրաշալի զյարութիւն).\n\n29. Tuesday. Tone 4 [BK]. Sons of Thunder. Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of the Nativity.\n\n30. Wednesday. Tone 5 [GDz]. Fast of the Nativity. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 8 [DK]: \"Blessed art Thou, Lord God, blessed\" (Օրհնեալ տէր աստուած օրհնեալ).\n\nJanuary:\n\n3. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADz]. Seventh [Sunday] of the Fast. Lord I Have Cried Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [Oy]: \"Awesome vision\" (Սոսկալի տեսիլ), to the end.\n\n5. Tuesday. Tone 3 [BDz]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ our God.\n\nNovember:\n\n1. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Eighth [Sunday]. Lord I Have Cried Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [AK]: \"The wondrous angel\" (Սքանչելի հրեշտակն).\n\n8. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADz]. Ninth [Sunday]. Lord I Have Cried Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [ODz]: \"With the women\" (Ընդ կանայսն), and \"Who Ineffable\" (Որ անճառ).\n\n15. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Tenth [Sunday]. Lord I Have Cried Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [DK]: \"Thy angel, O Lord\" (Հրեշտակ քո տէր), to the end. Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of the Advent [Yisnakats].\n\n16. Monday. Tone 1 [ADz]. Fast of the Advent. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] of Penitence Tone 5 [GDz]: \"Blessed art Thou forever\" (Օրհնեալ ես յաւիտեան).\n\n21. Saturday. Tone 6 [GK]. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God.\n\n22. Sunday. Tone 7 [DDz]. First [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 1 [ADz]: \"Blessed art Thou, Lord God\" (Օրհնեալ ես տէր աստուած). Lord I Have Cried Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [DDz]: \"Awesome\" (Ահագին), and \"Who art above\" (Որ ի վերդ ես).\n\n23. Monday. Tone 8 [DK]. Saints Julian and Vasilissa. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 7 [DDz]: \"Who [the torments]\" (Որք զտանջանս).\n\n29. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK]. Second [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 2 [AK]: \"Thy unoriginate Word\" (Անսկիզբն բանդ). Lord I Have Cried Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Receiving also our blessings\" (Առեալ եւ մեր զօրհնութիւնս).\n\nDecember:\n\n2. Wednesday. Tone 1 [ADz]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 8 [DK]: \"O God of our fathers, have mercy\" (Աստուած հարցն մերոց ողորմեա).\n\n5. Saturday. Tone 4 [BK]. Saints Nicholas, and Gregory the Wonderworker, Patriarchs; and the other Patriarch Nicholas, and Bishop Myron. Magnificat [Mankunk] on the note: \"They wondered\" (Հիացան). Morning hymn, Tone 3 [BDz]: \"Who with light\" (Որ լուսով).\n\n---\nTHE SEVEN-DAY CYCLE OF THE ROMANS IN JANUARY:\n\nJanuary:\n\n6. MONDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The duration of non-fasting days [Utis] is fourteen days.\n\n14. Tuesday. Saint John the Forerunner [Precursor].\n\n16. Thursday. Saint Peter the Patriarch, etc.\n\n18. Saturday. Saint Anthony the Hermit.\n\n19. Sunday. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 7 [DDz]: \"Dawn of the Only-begotten\" (Ծագումն միածնի). Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of the Catechumens [Arachavorats].\n\n26. Sunday. Saint Sarkis. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 5 [GDz]: \"Glorifying\" (Փառաւորելով). And see the others in order in the First Volume up to Transfiguration [Vardavar], keeping the order of the place.\n\nFebruary:\n\n9. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Real Barekendan [Quinquagesima Sunday].\n\n14. Friday. Tone 5 [GDz]. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndarach].",
